 Holy geez.

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:17.383
Oh, my God.

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.452
DOUG MARCAIDA: One of the most
intimidating and versatile

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.654
Japanese pole weapons,
the sodegarami,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:24.157
was part of the key
arsenal for samurai police

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.092
during the 17th century.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.193
Featuring lethal
spikes and hooks,

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.497
police were able to
capture violent offenders

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.398
from the distance
by using the weapon

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:36.335
to latch onto the suspects,
stopping them in their tracks.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.271
Although primarily
used in defense,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.573
the sharp spikes along
with the spiked bud cap

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:43.943
made it a menacing and
brutal weapon when in combat.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.379
Today, the sodegarami's
devastating use

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:50.149
can be seen in the HBO
television series, "Westworld."

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.920
All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

