 All right, come on forward
and shake our hands, my friend.

00:15:23.188 --> 00:15:24.890
KEATON: I'm a "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:15:24.957 --> 00:15:25.924
I did it.

00:15:26.024 --> 00:15:27.058
This experience has been great.

00:15:27.158 --> 00:15:28.326
It was definitely a challenge.

00:15:28.393 --> 00:15:29.995
The biggest thing I
took away from this

00:15:30.061 --> 00:15:32.631
was just work hard, keep
going, no matter what happens.

00:15:32.698 --> 00:15:42.407 line:14%
[music playing]

00:15:42.474 --> 00:15:43.342
HOST: The naginata.

00:15:46.445 --> 00:15:47.312
 [bleep].

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:48.280
All right.

00:15:48.347 --> 00:15:49.882
HOST: The naginata
emerged around

00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:52.584
1,000 years ago in Japan
as a powerful pole weapon

00:15:52.651 --> 00:15:54.353
used by samurai warriors.

00:15:54.419 --> 00:15:57.255
Featuring a single edged
slightly curved blade mounted

00:15:57.355 --> 00:15:59.924
on a wooden shaft,
this 7 to 8 foot weapon

00:15:59.991 --> 00:16:01.593
was ideal for
warding off attacks

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.395
from enemies on horseback.

00:16:03.495 --> 00:16:05.430
Because it relied on
momentum rather than

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:07.933
upper body strength,
it was an ideal weapon

00:16:08.033 --> 00:16:09.501
for female warriors.

00:16:09.568 --> 00:16:12.337
The naginata was the weapon
of choice for samurai wives

00:16:12.404 --> 00:16:14.105
defending their
homes, and was even

00:16:14.172 --> 00:16:16.808
wielded by Seong Menon
in the video game

00:16:16.875 --> 00:16:18.843
series "Soul Caliber."

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.779
The traditions of
the naginata continue

00:16:20.846 --> 00:16:23.382
to be preserved through the
teaching of the martial art,

00:16:23.449 --> 00:16:25.250
Atarashii Naginata.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:28.420
 The naginata was a Japanese
weapon known for its long range

00:16:28.487 --> 00:16:29.755
cutting ability.

00:16:29.821 --> 00:16:32.023
To see how sharp your naginata
is, I will take your weapon,

00:16:32.124 --> 00:16:34.093
and I'll attempt to cut
through these tatami mats

00:16:34.193 --> 00:16:35.327
and a side of beef.

00:16:35.394 --> 00:16:36.828
Theo, you're up first.
You ready?

00:16:36.895 --> 00:16:37.696
 Yeah.

00:16:37.796 --> 00:16:38.630
Yeah, I think so.

00:16:38.697 --> 00:16:39.965
 Let's do this.

00:16:40.032 --> 00:16:41.499
 Oh jeez.

00:16:41.566 --> 00:16:43.502
All right.

00:16:43.569 --> 00:16:47.539
[music playing]

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:51.809
I'll take it.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.177
Yeah, all right.

00:16:53.278 --> 00:16:54.312
 I just want to point
out that after that test,

00:16:54.413 --> 00:16:56.614
your blade has a
slight bend to it.

00:16:56.681 --> 00:16:59.651
It almost cut all the way
through one of the tatami mats.

00:16:59.717 --> 00:17:03.755
When it came to the side of
beef, it cut cleanly through.

00:17:03.855 --> 00:17:05.123
Your blade feels good.

00:17:05.223 --> 00:17:07.259
It's got a nice weight
to it, a nice balance.

00:17:07.325 --> 00:17:10.528
Overall, your naginata will cut.

00:17:10.595 --> 00:17:11.296
Good job.

00:17:11.363 --> 00:17:12.230
 Thank you.

00:17:12.297 --> 00:17:13.331
 Joe, you're up next.
You ready?

00:17:13.398 --> 00:17:13.999
 Oh yeah.

00:17:14.066 --> 00:17:15.700
Let's do this.

00:17:15.801 --> 00:17:19.638
[music playing]

00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:22.508
 Nice.

00:17:26.245 --> 00:17:28.213
Oh, well done, man.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:30.682
 Yeah.

00:17:30.783 --> 00:17:32.283
I would say I'm
ahead in the game.

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:35.287
I performed a little bit
better than what Theo's did.

00:17:43.061 --> 00:17:45.030
 Well Joe, you have
a very sharp blade,

00:17:45.097 --> 00:17:48.300
but we now have an issue.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:52.003
When I cut through the tatami
mat, your handle at the seams

00:17:52.104 --> 00:17:54.172
here came apart.

00:17:54.238 --> 00:17:58.476
Your handle seam has opened up.

00:17:58.543 --> 00:18:00.545
And not only that, it
picked up some cracks

00:18:00.645 --> 00:18:03.048
on this side that runs
all the way down here,

00:18:03.114 --> 00:18:05.517
and on the other side,
a hairline fracture

00:18:05.584 --> 00:18:06.952
that goes down this way.

00:18:07.019 --> 00:18:09.054
The seams are big enough
to where I can actually

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:11.289
put my fingernail through them.

00:18:11.356 --> 00:18:13.425
That is a critical failure.

00:18:13.525 --> 00:18:15.927
And for purposes of
safety, we cannot

00:18:15.993 --> 00:18:18.530
continue to test your weapon.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:19.198
 There's nothing?

00:18:19.298 --> 00:18:20.699
We can't do nothing?

00:18:20.799 --> 00:18:23.502
 Bladesmiths, the judges
have determined that there's

00:18:23.602 --> 00:18:25.270
no reason to deliberate.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.572
Joe, due to the
catastrophic failure

00:18:27.672 --> 00:18:31.610
of your weapon's handle,
you may now leave the arena.

00:18:38.116 --> 00:18:39.951
 It's not the way
I wanted to win.

00:18:40.051 --> 00:18:41.887
 I feel like I'm
in a round room

00:18:41.987 --> 00:18:44.022
and I'm looking for
a corner to cry in.

00:18:44.089 --> 00:18:46.858
It's a pretty tough loss.

00:18:46.958 --> 00:18:48.426
 Theo, congratulations.

00:18:48.493 --> 00:18:49.962
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:18:50.028 --> 00:18:52.897
and will be receiving
that $10,000 prize.

00:18:52.964 --> 00:18:53.931
Good job.

00:18:53.998 --> 00:18:57.069
[applauding]

00:18:57.135 --> 00:18:58.336
 You know what I
like about your blade?

00:18:58.436 --> 00:19:00.105
The way you reinforced
your handle.

00:19:00.172 --> 00:19:03.775
Because the power you
generate with that saved it.

00:19:03.841 --> 00:19:04.509
 Congratulations.

00:19:04.576 --> 00:19:05.744
 Thank you, sir.

00:19:05.811 --> 00:19:08.546
I am elated to be the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:19:08.613 --> 00:19:12.116
Not the way I wanted to
win, but I'll take it.

00:19:12.217 --> 00:19:17.055
I came here the youngest
smallest person and I won.

00:19:17.156 --> 00:19:19.957
For the shortest guy, I
certainly came out on top.

00:19:20.058 --> 00:19:23.896 line:14%
[music playing]

00:19:25.229 --> 00:19:28.199
 The Jumonji Yari.

00:19:28.299 --> 00:19:30.836
Originating in the
1500s, the Jumonji Yari

00:19:30.902 --> 00:19:34.071
was carried by Japanese
soldiers known as the ashigaru.

00:19:34.172 --> 00:19:35.674
These peasant foot
soldiers relied

00:19:35.774 --> 00:19:38.476
on the long shafted spear
for its reach and versatility

00:19:38.543 --> 00:19:39.811
in combat.

00:19:39.911 --> 00:19:42.814
Using the weapon's double edged
cross bars to disarm and pull

00:19:42.915 --> 00:19:44.449
mounted samurai
from their horses,

00:19:44.516 --> 00:19:47.920
the ashigaru could then employ
the razor sharp central blade

00:19:47.986 --> 00:19:49.922
to fatally skewer
the fallen enemy,

00:19:49.988 --> 00:19:51.623
and all from a
comfortable distance.

00:19:51.723 --> 00:19:54.258
Today, video game
enthusiasts can unleash

00:19:54.325 --> 00:19:56.828
the Jumonji Yari's
devastating capabilities

00:19:56.894 --> 00:19:58.597
in the game "Shadow Fight II."

00:19:58.663 --> 00:20:02.301
 The yari, with its long
handle and multi-pronged spear,

00:20:02.401 --> 00:20:07.239
makes it a trifecta of points
and edges and a deadly weapon.

00:20:07.306 --> 00:20:09.808
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:20:09.875 --> 00:20:12.043
I will take your yari and
deliver multiple slashes

00:20:12.109 --> 00:20:14.346
and thrust on this pig carcass.

00:20:14.446 --> 00:20:15.514
Fouad, you're up first.

00:20:15.581 --> 00:20:16.013
Are you ready?

00:20:16.114 --> 00:20:18.116
 Oh, I'm ready.

00:20:18.183 --> 00:20:22.287
[music playing]

00:20:28.593 --> 00:20:29.361
Jesus.

00:20:38.437 --> 00:20:40.672
 All right, Fouad, let's
talk about your yari here.

00:20:40.738 --> 00:20:43.975
We felt that it had
very good balance to it.

00:20:44.075 --> 00:20:49.080
That on the initial slash right
here, It dug in into flesh.

00:20:49.147 --> 00:20:50.581
Then it hit the spine.

00:20:50.681 --> 00:20:54.752
The transference of energy hit
a weak spot into your handle

00:20:54.819 --> 00:20:55.954
over here.

00:20:56.021 --> 00:21:00.024
But it still had a secondary
cut all the way through.

00:21:00.125 --> 00:21:03.828
I would consider
your blade a kill.

00:21:03.928 --> 00:21:05.030
 Thank you.

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:09.200
It was, mine was
beautiful well made.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.603
And some wood grain
just, you know.

00:21:14.572 --> 00:21:17.942
 Fouad, your weapon suffered
a catastrophic failure.

00:21:18.043 --> 00:21:19.277
Now that's bad.

00:21:19.344 --> 00:21:21.280
However, you're not out
of this competition yet.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:26.151
Jacob, your yari still must
perform in this kill test.

00:21:26.251 --> 00:21:27.552
Let's see what happens.

00:21:27.619 --> 00:21:30.989
 Right now, I'm
feeling nauseous.

00:21:31.055 --> 00:21:32.691
My heart's pounding in my chest.

00:21:32.758 --> 00:21:34.326
My hands are sweaty.

00:21:34.393 --> 00:21:41.866
And I just can't wait to see
how it actually goes down.

00:21:41.933 --> 00:21:45.937
[music playing]

00:22:02.019 --> 00:22:02.987
 All right, Jacob.

00:22:03.054 --> 00:22:04.522
Let's talk about your yari.

00:22:04.622 --> 00:22:07.525
In the initial swing, instead
of being able to cut cleanly

00:22:07.625 --> 00:22:10.995
with this part to cut
through, this got in the way

00:22:11.062 --> 00:22:12.530
with the angle that it had.

00:22:12.630 --> 00:22:15.000
But let's talk about
these particular blades.

00:22:15.066 --> 00:22:18.804
They are sharp enough to
penetrate into the pig carcass.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:23.641
The thrust is really devastating
and very deep into that.

00:22:23.741 --> 00:22:27.779
Your handle construction,
it stayed true.

00:22:27.879 --> 00:22:29.180
No issues at all.

00:22:29.246 --> 00:22:31.983
Overall, your weapon will kill.

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.652
 Thank you, sir.

00:22:33.719 --> 00:22:35.320
My yari held up.

00:22:35.386 --> 00:22:38.723
And I'm just-- thank you God.

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:41.092
 Well Fouad, the
blades of your yari

00:22:41.192 --> 00:22:43.228
were beautifully constructed.

00:22:43.294 --> 00:22:45.296
The overall weapon
was very elegant.

00:22:45.396 --> 00:22:48.566
However, your shaft
broke in our first test.

00:22:48.633 --> 00:22:50.168
And we cannot move
forward in this

00:22:50.268 --> 00:22:55.307
competition because that is a
catastrophic weapon failure.

00:22:55.407 --> 00:22:56.975
And I have to ask you to
please leave the forge.

00:22:57.075 --> 00:22:59.777
 I was really confident
going into the competition.

00:22:59.844 --> 00:23:03.515
I felt like my yari was
going to really perform

00:23:03.615 --> 00:23:05.150
a lot better than Jacob's.

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:08.886
And it's just pure
irony all the way down.

00:23:08.953 --> 00:23:11.690
 Jacob, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion

00:23:11.756 --> 00:23:14.092
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:23:14.159 --> 00:23:15.793
Good job.

00:23:15.860 --> 00:23:17.428
[applauding]

00:23:17.495 --> 00:23:19.030
How do you feel right now?

00:23:19.097 --> 00:23:20.632
 I feel amazing.

00:23:20.698 --> 00:23:23.835
I came here to prove that I can
actually come out here at 19

00:23:23.935 --> 00:23:26.070
and compete with
serious knife makers.

00:23:26.171 --> 00:23:27.739
Thank you, sir.

00:23:27.806 --> 00:23:30.308
Really, I would have liked to
beat Fouad in a different way.

00:23:30.375 --> 00:23:32.977
But I'm the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:23:33.044 --> 00:23:36.247
$10,000?

00:23:36.314 --> 00:23:37.948
It's awesome.

00:23:38.049 --> 00:23:41.920 line:14%
[music playing]

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:47.626
HOST: The Japanese katana.

00:23:47.692 --> 00:23:49.661
The katana is the
traditional weapon

00:23:49.761 --> 00:23:52.597
of the samurai, the noble
class of warriors in feudal

00:23:52.664 --> 00:23:55.367
Japan since around 800 AD.

00:23:55.434 --> 00:23:58.035
The katana was formed from
hundreds of thin layers

00:23:58.135 --> 00:23:59.671
of the purest steel available.

00:23:59.771 --> 00:24:02.440
The quicker draw of the sword
was well suited to combat,

00:24:02.507 --> 00:24:04.876
where life versus death
depended on the weapon

00:24:04.943 --> 00:24:06.211
you carried into battle.

00:24:06.311 --> 00:24:07.779
Over the centuries,
the katana has

00:24:07.879 --> 00:24:09.581
taken on many
mythical properties

00:24:09.647 --> 00:24:11.749
in legend and culture,
from an ability

00:24:11.816 --> 00:24:14.319
to slice through other
swords to splitting a hair.

00:24:14.386 --> 00:24:16.455
And it is the sword of
choice for characters

00:24:16.521 --> 00:24:19.391
in mega-hits like "Kill
Bill" and "The Walking Dead."

00:24:19.458 --> 00:24:22.827
To measure how your blades
stand up against flesh,

00:24:22.894 --> 00:24:25.230
Doug will cut
through these fish.

00:24:25.296 --> 00:24:26.598
Rich, yours is up.

00:24:26.698 --> 00:24:29.234
Let's put it to the test.

00:24:29.301 --> 00:24:33.472
[music playing]

00:24:46.250 --> 00:24:48.319
 Nice.

00:24:48.386 --> 00:24:49.521
 It will cut.

00:24:49.588 --> 00:24:51.022
 Yes, it will.

00:24:51.089 --> 00:24:54.425
 It felt good in the slice.

00:24:54.492 --> 00:24:55.827
The recovery was
a little heavier,

00:24:55.927 --> 00:24:59.731
but it still felt like
it'll give me a close shave.

00:24:59.798 --> 00:25:01.132
Good job.

00:25:01.199 --> 00:25:01.899
OK, Matt.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:02.433
You're up next.

00:25:02.534 --> 00:25:03.267
Are you ready?

00:25:03.334 --> 00:25:05.035
 Yeah.

00:25:05.136 --> 00:25:09.140
[music playing]

00:25:18.550 --> 00:25:19.751
It doesn't cut.

00:25:19.817 --> 00:25:21.252
I'm a little confused by that.

00:25:21.352 --> 00:25:22.854
I don't know why it didn't cut.

00:25:31.529 --> 00:25:32.930
 It's got a very
good feel to it.

00:25:33.031 --> 00:25:33.898
It's very light.

00:25:33.965 --> 00:25:35.933
It's got a very
nice balance to it.

00:25:36.034 --> 00:25:40.672
And it'll cut.

00:25:40.772 --> 00:25:42.706
Now for the kill test.

00:25:42.807 --> 00:25:44.708
In this, we have
a ballistics dummy

00:25:44.809 --> 00:25:47.945
that pretty much simulates
the human form, organs,

00:25:48.012 --> 00:25:49.080
and tissues.

00:25:49.147 --> 00:25:52.551
The katana traditionally
has a razor sharp edge.

00:25:52.617 --> 00:25:56.688
That allows me to find the
gaps in between the armor.

00:25:56.755 --> 00:25:59.657
I'm going to try that with your
blade to see how well it does.

00:25:59.724 --> 00:26:02.126
Rich, you're up first.

00:26:02.193 --> 00:26:06.197
[music playing]

00:26:23.747 --> 00:26:24.983
Let's take a look at the damage.

00:26:28.520 --> 00:26:31.522
The thrust and the slice
went all the way into

00:26:31.589 --> 00:26:33.724
the internal organs in here.

00:26:33.791 --> 00:26:39.397
And the kill shot went deep,
all the way into the liver.

00:26:39.497 --> 00:26:44.168
I think on the kill
test, this will kill.

00:26:44.235 --> 00:26:44.969
OK, Matt.

00:26:45.036 --> 00:26:47.305
You're up.

00:26:47.372 --> 00:26:51.343
[music playing]

00:27:10.495 --> 00:27:11.696
Definitely through
the laceration,

00:27:11.796 --> 00:27:13.598
he's disemboweled here.

00:27:13.664 --> 00:27:16.467
And a nice big puncture in here.

00:27:16.534 --> 00:27:19.671
That definitely
will get the liver.

00:27:19.771 --> 00:27:22.039
I think it's passed
the kill test.

00:27:22.106 --> 00:27:23.408
 Thank you.

00:27:23.474 --> 00:27:27.845
 You both obviously brought
deadly implements of war here.

00:27:27.912 --> 00:27:30.881
But now, it's time to
lock and load, gentlemen.

00:27:30.981 --> 00:27:34.418
Because for the strength
test, we're leaving the forge

00:27:34.518 --> 00:27:36.454
and we're heading
to the gun range.

00:27:36.554 --> 00:27:37.322
 What?

00:27:42.827 --> 00:27:44.395
 All right, gentlemen.

00:27:44.462 --> 00:27:48.365
This is the final test for the
"Forged in Fire" championship.

00:27:48.432 --> 00:27:50.000
It's the strength test.

00:27:50.100 --> 00:27:52.770
Your weapons will be
tested on their ability

00:27:52.870 --> 00:27:54.539
to split a bullet.

00:27:54.606 --> 00:27:57.876
Your swords are going to
be locked into a vise.

00:27:57.976 --> 00:28:00.679
Then we're going to fire
a bullet at your blade.

00:28:03.715 --> 00:28:04.582
All right, Matt.

00:28:04.649 --> 00:28:05.917
You ready?

00:28:05.984 --> 00:28:06.685
 Break it.

00:28:11.122 --> 00:28:13.524
 3, 2, 1.

00:28:13.591 --> 00:28:15.326
Engage.

00:28:15.393 --> 00:28:16.527
[cheering]

00:28:16.594 --> 00:28:17.362
 Yes!

00:28:21.433 --> 00:28:24.735
 Matt, your sword
split a bullet.

00:28:24.802 --> 00:28:27.138
There's no damage
on the edge at all.

00:28:27.205 --> 00:28:28.239
Held up extremely well.

00:28:28.306 --> 00:28:31.241
That is a real true sign
of your craftsmanship.

00:28:31.308 --> 00:28:31.743
 Thank you.

00:28:31.810 --> 00:28:33.077
 Very well done.

00:28:33.144 --> 00:28:33.811
All right.

00:28:33.878 --> 00:28:35.312
Rich, you're up next.

00:28:35.412 --> 00:28:38.016
 When I look at him set the
gun up and get ready to shoot

00:28:38.082 --> 00:28:40.518
that blade, there's
a little bit of doubt

00:28:40.618 --> 00:28:41.719
in the back of my mind.

00:28:41.786 --> 00:28:43.688
Thinking it may
not survive this.

00:28:43.755 --> 00:28:46.357
 3, 2, 1.

00:28:46.424 --> 00:28:47.558
Engage.

00:28:47.625 --> 00:28:48.359
Nice!

00:28:48.426 --> 00:28:49.627
 Oh yeah!

00:28:49.694 --> 00:28:50.462
Straight.

00:28:53.531 --> 00:28:54.465
Wow.

00:28:54.565 --> 00:28:56.267
That is a real split there.

00:28:56.367 --> 00:28:57.134
 Nice.

00:28:57.201 --> 00:28:58.002
 I like it.

00:28:58.102 --> 00:28:59.537
 That blade didn't even move.

00:28:59.637 --> 00:29:01.572
 It splits the bullet.

00:29:01.638 --> 00:29:02.973
I couldn't have been happier.

00:29:03.040 --> 00:29:05.243
 There's no mark
on the blade at all.

00:29:05.309 --> 00:29:06.577
Held up perfectly.

00:29:06.677 --> 00:29:08.312
No chipping.

00:29:08.379 --> 00:29:09.680
Everything looks great.

00:29:09.747 --> 00:29:11.382
 Thank you.

00:29:11.482 --> 00:29:12.817
 Congratulations, gentlemen.

00:29:12.884 --> 00:29:14.853
You should be proud of
the work that you've done.

00:29:14.953 --> 00:29:18.389
Which only makes the judges'
decision that much harder.

00:29:18.455 --> 00:29:20.591
We'll see you back at the forge.

00:29:20.658 --> 00:29:25.196
Matt, Rich, in
just five days, you

00:29:25.263 --> 00:29:29.600
have both forged elegant
and lethal Japanese katanas.

00:29:29.667 --> 00:29:31.035
But in this
competition, there can

00:29:31.135 --> 00:29:33.771
only be one winner of $10,000.

00:29:33.838 --> 00:29:40.177
Matt, you are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:29:40.278 --> 00:29:42.312
Congratulations.

00:29:42.413 --> 00:29:43.814
 Good job, dude.

00:29:43.915 --> 00:29:46.317
 Rich, you did
not make the cut.

00:29:46.383 --> 00:29:48.820
 I wish you had done a little
bit more finishing work.

00:29:48.886 --> 00:29:51.055
 You let the handle
get a little bit skinny.

00:29:51.121 --> 00:29:54.091
And it was almost the same
proportions on each side.

00:29:54.191 --> 00:29:56.694
So I know you ran into
a time constraint.

00:29:56.794 --> 00:29:58.796
But it did split a
bullet, and that's

00:29:58.896 --> 00:30:00.398
truly something to be proud of.

00:30:00.465 --> 00:30:06.437
 I feel a little disappointed,
but the better bladesmith won.

00:30:06.503 --> 00:30:08.606
 Well, Matt, congratulations.

00:30:08.706 --> 00:30:10.208
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:30:10.274 --> 00:30:12.443
You're going to claim
a $10,000 check.

00:30:12.510 --> 00:30:13.644
How do you feel?

00:30:13.744 --> 00:30:14.946
 This is awesome.

00:30:15.046 --> 00:30:16.747
 Your blade is beautiful.

00:30:16.814 --> 00:30:18.816
Not only is it
beautiful, but it's fast.

00:30:18.916 --> 00:30:20.451
Cut so cleanly through the fish.

00:30:20.551 --> 00:30:22.820
And on the ballistic dummy,
that just disemboweled it

00:30:22.920 --> 00:30:23.788
for the kill test.

00:30:23.855 --> 00:30:24.922
Great job.

00:30:24.989 --> 00:30:26.523
 Blade aside, I
was really impressed

00:30:26.590 --> 00:30:27.658
with your handle set up.

00:30:27.724 --> 00:30:28.860
Symmetrically, it was correct.

00:30:28.960 --> 00:30:30.862
We get good control,
good grip on it.

00:30:30.928 --> 00:30:32.363
Very nicely done.

00:30:32.463 --> 00:30:34.198
 This is such a rush.

00:30:34.265 --> 00:30:36.167
I want to drive home
and kiss my son.

00:30:36.234 --> 00:30:38.536
I'm the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:30:38.603 --> 00:30:40.972 line:14%
[music playing]

